<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-April nickel output slips, aluminium up.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-April nickel output slips, aluminium up.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian nickel production fell two percent in the first four months of 1997 against year-ago levels, while primary aluminium output edged up one percent, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The committee gave no absolute production figures, but provided the following data --  </p>
<p>RUSSIA JAN-APRIL 97 NON-FERROUS, PRECIOUS, MINOR METALS OUTPUT</p>
<p>(all figures expressed as percentage of previous corresponding period)</p>
<p>				  April 1997	 Jan-April 1997</p>
<p>				  pct change	   pct change</p>
<p>				   mth/mth		  yr/yr</p>
<p> Alumina			   106		     98</p>
<p> Primary aluminium	     102		    101</p>
<p> Bauxite			   119		     87</p>
<p> Copper concentrate	     84		     82</p>
<p> Refined copper		  104		     93</p>
<p> Nickel			    101		     98</p>
<p> Cobalt			     83		     93</p>
<p> Zinc				 99		    103</p>
<p> Lead (incl. secondary)	112		    271</p>
<p> Gold				124		    126</p>
<p> Magnesium (and alloys)	103		    102</p>
<p> Titanium sponge		 104		    155</p>
<p> Rolled aluminium		107		     86</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
